in $\vdcat{A}$, where $i_{k-1}=(s_{k})_-$ and $i_k=(s_k)_{+}$ for each $1\leq k\leq n$.
(When $n=0$, we identify the set $S_1\times_{I_1}S_2\times_{I_2}\dots\times_{I_{n-1}}S_n$ with $I_0$, and hence $\vect{\alpha}$ is an $I_0$-indexed family of multicells of $\vdcat{A}$.)
\end{itemize}

\begin{proposition}
    The $2$-functor $\FFam\colon \VDbl\to \VDbl$ is familial.
\end{proposition}
\begin{proof}
    This follows from \cref{prop:poly-familial,dof-between-vdbl-is-internal-dof}.
\end{proof}

The left $2$-adjoint of the $2$-functor $\FFam_1\colon \VDbl\to \VDbl/\SSpan$ (which is the composite of the first two factors of \cref{eqn:FFam-composite}) is 
