%-----------------------------------------------------------------
\subsection{Conformal Cartan Geometry}
\label{app:conformal_cartan}

Let \(G=\mathrm{SO}(4,2)\) be the four-dimensional conformal group and
\(P\subset G\) its parabolic subgroup that stabilises a null ray.  A
\emph{conformal Cartan geometry} on a smooth spacetime \(M\) is a
principal \(P\)-bundle \(\pi:\mathcal P\to M\) endowed with a
\(\mathfrak g\)-valued 1-form
\[
A\;\in\;\Omega^{1}\!\bigl(\mathcal P;\,\mathfrak g\bigr)
\]
that is (i) an isomorphism
\(T_{p}\mathcal P\xrightarrow{\;\simeq\;}\mathfrak g\) at every
\(p\in\mathcal P\), (ii) \(P\)-equivariant
\(R_{a}^{*}A=\operatorname{Ad}(a^{-1})A\), and (iii) reproduces the
generators of the right action: \(A(\zeta^{*})=\zeta\) for all
\(\zeta\in\mathfrak p\).

The \(|1|\)-grading
\(\mathfrak g=\mathfrak p_{-1}\oplus\mathfrak p_{0}\oplus\mathfrak p_{1}\)
decomposes the Cartan connection into
\[
A=e^{\mu}P_{\mu}+\omega^{\mu\nu}M_{\mu\nu}+b\,D+f^{\mu}K_{\mu},
\]
where \(e^{\mu}\) is the solder form, \(\omega^{\mu\nu}\) the spin
connection, \(b\) the Weyl (dilational) gauge field, and \(f^{\mu}\)
the special-conformal gauge field.

\paragraph{Gauge fixing to the block–homothetic subgroup.}
From now on we \emph{freeze a future-directed timelike (equivalently\,:
a null) ray in} \(\mathbb R^{4,2}\).  On the base \(M\) that choice
projects to the \emph{fixed vector}
\(X_{d}\!\in\!TM\) introduced in
Section \ref{section:2-First setup}.  The remaining structure group is
the semidirect product
\(H=\mathrm{SO}(3,1)\ltimes\mathbb R\); its \(\mathbb R\) factor acts
by the block-upper-triangular matrices
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:Lambda-def-app}
\Lambda[\lambda](x)=
\begin{pmatrix}
e^{-\lambda(x)} & 1-e^{-\lambda(x)}\\[2pt]
0 & 1
\end{pmatrix},
\qquad \lambda\in C^{\infty}(M).
\end{equation}
On a weight-zero tractor
\(V=\bigl(V~~V_{d}\bigr)^{\!\top}\) this reads
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:tractor-action}
\Lambda[\lambda](x)\cdot V=
\begin{pmatrix}
e^{-\lambda(x)}\,V+\bigl(1-e^{-\lambda(x)}\bigr)V_{d}\\[2pt]
V_{d}
\end{pmatrix},
\end{equation}
which reproduces Eq. (\ref{eq:homothetic-u}) when we put \(V\mapsto X\) and
\(V_{d}\mapsto X_{d}\).

\paragraph{Associated bundles and differential forms.}
Because every representation of \(P\) (and hence of
\(H\subset P\)) yields an associated bundle, all fields used in the
main text acquire a natural Cartan meaning:
\begin{itemize}
\item vector fields of homothetic weight \(w\) are sections of
      \(\mathcal P\times_{P}\mathbb R^{1,3}[w]\);
\item \(p\)-forms of weight \(w\) are sections of
      \(\mathcal P\times_{P}\!\bigl(\Lambda^{p}\mathfrak p_{-1}^{*}\bigr)[w]\);
\item the doubled bundle \(TM\oplus TM\) of
      Section \ref{section:2-First setup} is the direct sum of two
      tractor bundles carrying weights \(0\) and \(-1\),
      respectively.
\end{itemize}
Hence all operators in $\S$ \ref{section:2-First setup} are functorial in
Cartan geometry.

