\emph{Why low turnover matters beyond cost.}  
QSW’s subdued trading footprint additionally mitigates

\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*),leftmargin=*]
\item \textbf{Price pressure} — smaller orders move prices less;
\item \textbf{Timing risk} — executions complete within a single session;
\item \textbf{Information leakage} — a lighter footprint is harder for
      liquidity-seeking algorithms to detect.
\end{enumerate}

These frictions compound rapidly for large mandates or in
liquidity-constrained universes, making the quantum engine’s naturally
low-turnover profile a \emph{structural} implementation advantage.





