      (\(+0.22\)), yet its impact on Sharpe itself remains small
      ( \(\pm0.04\) ).  In other words, tightening the transaction-cost
      prior is an almost ‘‘free’’ way to push portfolios leftwards on the
      cost–efficiency frontier.

\item \textbf{\(\omega\) (quantum–classical mix):}  
