\section{Computing $\tol((x-a)^2(x-b)(x-c))$}\label{sec:code}
Primarily for our own reference, we include the Sage code that we used to express $\tol((x-a)^2(x-b)(x-c))$ in terms of the coefficients of this polynomial. The input \texttt{m = [2,1,1]} signifies the partition of multiplicities of roots for $f$. This can be replaced with any other partition, although the computational time grows quickly as the length of \texttt{m} increases.

There are cases where this code outputs a vector of rational (rather than integer) coefficients, such as for \texttt{m = [4,3]}. This could probably be resolved by rephrasing things in terms of Sage's \texttt{IntegerLattice} functionality, but we will not do this here. The alternative is that the formula for $\tol((x-a)^4(x-b)^3)$ in terms of the coefficients of $(x-a)^4(x-b)^3$ legitimately requires rational coefficients, which would be an interesting deviation from the case of discriminants.
\begin{lstlisting}
