\subsection{Image crop from ground tiles}  \label{sec:image_crop_from_ground}

Thanks to the RPC camera model~\cite{rpc_sar}, we can project points from the 3D space to image coordinates. For each 3D tile and each input image, we create a crop of the images containing the projections of the 8 corners of the 3D tile. To limit the memory footprint, when processing a set of tiles, we will load only the corresponding NeRFs and crops. This approach guarantees that the 3D tile of each loaded NeRF is fully covered by the loaded images (see Figure~\ref{fig:3D_partition_merge_tuilage_from_roi}). This alleviates the need to fully load an entire large image into memory at any moment, something that is commonly overlooked in NeRF pipelines. 
