commutes. For any $a \in A$, we have that $ s(0_{B})\rightarrow a \in X$, since 
\[
p(s(0_{B})\rightarrow a)=ps(0_{B})\rightarrow p(a)=0_{B}\rightarrow p(a)=1.
\]
It follows that $(s(0_{B})\rightarrow a,1) \in UM(X)$. Moreover
\begin{align*}
1=f(1,1)=f((1,0)\rightarrow (s(0_{B})\rightarrow a,1))&=f(1,0)\rightarrow f(s(0_{B})\rightarrow a,1)\\
&=(f \circ UM(\iota))(0)\rightarrow (f \circ \eta_{X})(s(0_{B})\rightarrow a)\\
&=s(0_{B})\rightarrow (s(0_{B})\rightarrow a)\\
&=(s(0_{B})\cdot s(0_{B}))\rightarrow a\\
&=s(0_{B}\cdot 0_{B})\rightarrow a\\
