    The $X$-coloring matrices of these virtual knotoids are the same,
    \[\mathcal{M}_X(3.1.1)=\left[\begin{array}{c c c}
		1 & 0 & 0 \\
        0 & 1 & 0 \\
        0 & 0 & 1
	\end{array}\right]= \mathcal{M}_X(3.1.3).\]
    Consider the biquandle virtual bracket given in Example \ref{mbvb}. Our Python computations show that the $X$-virtual bracket matrices of these virtual knotoid diagrams are as follows.
    \[\mathcal{M}_X^{\beta}(3.1.1)=\left[\begin{array}{c c c}
		u^2 & 0 & 0 \\
        0 & u^2 & 0 \\
        0 & 0 & u^2
	\end{array}\right],\qquad \mathcal{M}_X^{\beta}(3.1.3)=\left[\begin{array}{c c c}
		u^3 & 0 & 0 \\
        0 & u^3 & 0 \\
        0 & 0 & u^2
	\end{array}\right].\]
