The Mie-Gr\"uneisen equation of state with shock Hugoniot as a reference is used as the equation of state for the sand:
$$P = P_{ref} + \gamma\rho(e - e_{ref}),$$
\begin{equation*}
	P_{ref} = \begin{cases}
		\rho_0 c_a^2\frac{1-x}{1-s_a(1-x)}, \, x\leq 1,
		\\
		\rho_0 c_a^2(1-x), \, x >1,
	\end{cases}
	e_{ref} = \begin{cases}
		\frac{1}{2}\left[\frac{c_a(1-x)}{1-s_a(1-x)}\right]^2, \, x\leq 1,
		\\
		c_a^2(1-x)^2/2, \, x >1,
	\end{cases}
	x = \frac{\rho_0}{\rho}.
\end{equation*}
Here $\rho_0 = 1674\,$ kg/m$^3$, $c_a = 1280\,$m/s, $\gamma = 2.17$, $s_a = 1.49$.

