	\section{Euchromatin activity}
	%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

	We now examine the case of nonzero euchromatin activity strength $\alpha$, focusing on positive values that correspond to extensile active stresses, while keeping the same three-dimensional periodic domain of side length $L$. In addition to the instability driven by contractile stresses (controlled by $\bar{\rho}_C$), this activity  introduces a distinct linear instability governed by the activity parameter $\alpha$.
