\subsection{Granularity Comparison}
We compared the strength and characteristics of lead-lag relationships across different data granularities. Our analysis reveals several important patterns:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Lead-lag effects are strongest at the 1-minute granularity and progressively weaken at coarser granularities
    \item At the 1-minute level, significant correlations extend to lags of 1-4 minutes for most pairs
    \item By the 15-minute level, only the strongest relationships remain statistically significant
    \item At the daily level, most intraday lead-lag relationships disappear entirely
\end{itemize}

This pattern suggests that the lead-lag effects we observe primarily reflect short-term information transmission or trading dynamics rather than fundamental economic relationships between firms.

