For varying stencil sizes, as illustrated in Figure \ref{adpative}, SparStencil consistently outperforms dense baselines across all stencil sizes and TCU fragments, achieving up to $4.1$× speedup and maintaining sparsity below $60\%$. Heatmaps show that optimal compute density emerges in specific $(r_1, r_2)$ regions, which are effectively discovered by our automated search. demonstrating the system’s ability to adaptively align diverse stencil patterns with TCU-efficient layouts.

