\section*{Data availability}
With the exception of the mobile phone metadata, all data used in this paper are publicly available and sources have been listed in the text. The mobile phone dataset contains detailed information on over 20 billion mobile phone transactions in Afghanistan. These data contain proprietary and confidential information belonging to a private telecommunications operator, and cannot be publicly released. Upon reasonable request, we can provide information to accredited academic researchers about how to request the proprietary data from the telecommunications operator. With the telecommunication operator's permission, we can also provide district-level aggregate measures of migration for replication purposes to accredited academic researchers.

\section*{Code availability}
All code to reproduce the findings of this study is available at \url{https://github.com/Global-Policy-Lab/afghanistan-civil-conflict-and-labor-flows}.

