\paragraph*{\S\ref{sec:Fu} -- Fusion rings.} After recalling some foundational concepts in~\S\ref{sub:Fu}, this section reviews the notion of formal codegrees in~\S\ref{sub:formal}, presenting two Egyptian fraction decompositions summing to one in the noncommutative setting. In~\S\ref{sub:Drin}, we introduce the notion of Drinfeld rings, motivated by properties of the formal codegrees arising in the Grothendieck ring of a pseudo-unitary fusion category. Finally,~\S\ref{sub:ext} discusses a universal construction for extending an integral fusion ring.

