There is a unique possible induction matrix (see Remark~\ref{rk:collected}), embedding~$\mathcal{C}$ into its Drinfeld center~$\mathcal{Z}(\mathcal{C})$, which has rank~$16$ and type $t = [[1,2], [2,1], [6,8], [14,3], [21,2]].$ This embedding induces a braiding on~$\mathcal{C}$, but no premodular fusion category of type~$[1,1,2,6]$ exists, by~\cite[Theorem 4.11]{B16}.
