As established in \S\ref{sec:Odd}, the Grothendieck ring of any odd-dimensional integral fusion category over~$\mathbb{C}$ is an MNSD integral Drinfeld ring (Definition~\ref{def:MNSDring}). This section provides a complete classification of such rings up to rank~$9$. %\textcolor{blue}{Finish the non-1-Frob at rank 9, and start the 1-Frob at rank 11}.

