\section{Noncommutative integral Drinfeld rings} \label{sec:NCA} 
Recall from Proposition~\ref{prop:min6} that $6$ is the smallest possible rank for a noncommutative fusion ring. This section provides a complete list of all $1 + 3 + 25$ noncommutative integral Drinfeld rings of rank at most~$8$. The corresponding data can be found in the files \verb|InvestNCRank6DataOnly.txt|, \verb|InvestNCRank7DataOnly.txt|, and \verb|InvestNCRank8DataOnly.txt|, located in the \verb|Data/Noncommutative| directory of~\cite{CodeData}. 

Note that the notation $m_n$ for a formal codegree indicates a value equal to $m$ arising from an $n$-dimensional irreducible representation. For simplicity, $m_1$ is written as $m$.

