Finally, we show upper bounds on the sensitivity of $\sre$ to string operations.\footnote{For the multiplicative sensitivity, we assume $w$ and $w'$ are not unary strings, as otherwise $\sre(w)$ or $\sre(w')$ would be $0$. This does not happen with $\chi$.} % the other hand, $\chi > \sigma$.}

\begin{lemma}Let $w\in \Sigma^*$  and $w' \in \mathtt{ins}_\Sigma(w) \cup \mathtt{del}_\Sigma(w) \cup \mathtt{sub}_\Sigma(w) \cup \rot(w) \cup \{w^R\}$. It holds
\begin{align*}
&\sre(w') - \sre(w) = O\left(\delta\max\left(1, \log(n/\delta\log \delta)\right)\log \delta\right) \text{ and } \\ 
&\sre(w')\hspace{3pt}/\hspace{4pt}\sre(w) = O\left(\max\left(1, \log(n/\delta\log \delta)\right)\log \delta\right).
\end{align*}
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
It follows because the multiplicative sensitivity of $\delta$ to the string operations considered and reversals
